      "settings": {
        "section_label": "Why Otto Exists",
        "quote": "Mahjong does what almost nothing else does — it blocks the outside world. Not by demanding you ignore it, but by requiring so much of you that there's simply no room left for it.",
        "body_1": "I came to Mahjong late. My sister taught me, sitting across a table that had been in her house for years. Within twenty minutes I understood why. The game is cognitively demanding in the best way — pattern recognition, flexible strategy, constrained creativity. It mirrors how I think when I'm designing.",
        "body_2": "What I couldn't find was a set that matched the feeling — or the room, or the people in it. The sets that existed were beautiful, but they weren't built for my home, my partner, or the way I wanted to use them. Otto is the set I wanted to buy and couldn't. Every component designed together, as one object. Calm. Considered. Built to stay on the table.",
